course: dictionary
lesson: 15706
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Topped is one of them. To find out which meaning is right, look at the words around it. «The pancakes were topped with strawberries and cream.» Here topped means covered on top with something.
explain: Topped can also mean went higher than a number, or beat it. «The temperature topped 30 degrees today.» The temperature did not sit on top of 30 degrees. It went above it. Numbers and news often use topped this way.
explain: Topped up means filled again to the top. «Dad topped up the car's tank at the petrol station.» Check by swapping in your meaning: Dad filled the tank again to the top. That makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Topped is also the past form of the verb top, so you may see top, tops, topping. When you see a phrase like topped the charts or topped the list, the phrase often gives the meaning away.
fact: Topped is the past form of the verb top: top, tops, topped, topping.
fact: «Topped with» means covered on top with something, like «a cake topped with cream».
fact: «Topped» can mean went higher than or beat, like «sales topped a million».
fact: «Topped up» means filled again to the top.
fact: «Topped the charts» means reached number one in the music charts, and «topped the list» means was first on the list.
exercise: «The hot chocolate was topped with little marshmallows.» What does topped mean here? | *Covered on top with something | Filled again to the top | Went higher than | Cut into small pieces
exercise: «Her score topped 900 points.» What does topped mean here? | *Went higher than | Covered on top with something | Filled again to the top | Slipped under
exercise: Which phrase means filled again to the top? | Topped the charts | *Topped up | Topped the list | Topped with
test: «Her song topped the charts for three weeks.» What does topped the charts mean? | Was filled to the brim with water | Climbed up a steep hill | Was covered with sweets | *Was at number one in the music charts
test: Which word is the past form of the verb top? | topper | tops | topping | *topped
exam: «The kettle was topped up before we made the tea.» What does topped up mean? | Put on the lid | Covered on top with tea | *Filled again to the top | Went higher than the kettle
